  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Light isolated rain showers with some\nembedded thunderstorms over central and eastern Nevada will\ncontinue into the evening hours and dissipate to clearer skies as\nthe upper level trough begins to weaken and starts to move northeast\ninto Utah by early Wednesday morning. As the upper level trough\nmoves out of Nevada, another very broad upper level trough forms\nbehind the main trough that will be centralized more towards\nsouthern California. This will aid in keeping flow pattern over\nNevada to a more west/southwest flow that will bring a gradual\nwarming in temperatures through the week with highs reaching back\ninto the 80s by Thursday. Winds will also be affected, staying at\na light to moderately breezy winds up to 5-15 mph, with some gusts\nreaching up to 20 mph. As the weekend approaches, a stronger more\ndefined trough to the northwest along the US-Canadian border will\npush through the northwestern CONUS as the broad upper level\ntrough to the south weakens. The stronger trough to the northwest\nwill extend into Nevada with cooler temperatures, as highs\nexpected to cool down into the 60s to 70s over the weekend.\nUnfortunately, calm, dry weather conditions will be the dominant\nweather event through the week as precipitation is not expected \nwith any of these additional upper troughs over Nevada as there \nisn't much moisture involved in these systems. \n\nEnd of the weekend and into next week, models are showing a third\nupper level trough moving into the western coast with increasing\nconfidence that it will extend south over Nevada. Confidence as to\nthe strength and timing begin to wane. At the same time, models\nare also showing Hurricane Polo (weakening to a tropical storm)\nwill move along the Pacific Coast in western Mexico and push into\nthe southwest. Confidence remains low at this time as the timing\nand position of the storm differ within the models with some\nindicating it approaching early next week, while others suggest it\ncoming later next week and weakening even further before crossing\ninto the US.",
